{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj'","aggregated_output":"(ns d2-wedge-probe2\n  \"H3-1 wedge diagnostic, round 2: drive the REAL kernel-c semantic path.\n\n  Round 1's probe (test/d2_wedge_probe.clj) never queued the fixture onto\n  the session medium — `tu/make-observer-session` mints an EMPTY medium and\n  the probe called no queue variant — so its evaluator-session drive was\n  vacuous: a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true` (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm)\n  before any step, and run-on-stream over an empty medium loads nothing and\n  runs nothing. Stage A below reproduces that drive and measures its step\n  count to confirm the false negative.\n\n  Stage B re-measures the exact kernel-c semantic path —\n  `yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine`'s semantic branch\n  (tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! + observer/run-on-stream +\n  run-bounded over vm/step) — instrumented at vm/step (count, wall time,\n  machine entering each step) and at the run-on-stream boundary (ready\n  checks, batches loaded, run entries with per-run step deltas), with a\n  watchdog that separates the three failure shapes:\n\n    - BUDGET-THROWN   run-bounded's 2M exhaustion throw reaches the caller\n    - WEDGE-IN-STEP   step count frozen: one vm/step never returns; the\n                      worker stack trace plus the entering machine are dumped\n    - RATE-COLLAPSE   steps still advance but steps/sec decays toward zero;\n                      the per-tick rate table plus a final snapshot are dumped\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\n(def ^:private original-run-on-stream observer/run-on-stream)\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- instrumentation\n\n(def steps (atom 0))\n(def in-step-nanos (atom 0))\n(def recent-durations (atom []))          ;; last 64 step durations, nanos\n(def last-machine (volatile! nil))        ;; machine entering the latest step\n(def load-count (atom 0))\n(def ready-count (atom 0))\n(def run-log (atom []))                   ;; one entry per run-on-stream `run`\n(def start-ms (atom nil))\n\n(defn- reset-instrumentation!\n  []\n  (reset! steps 0)\n  (reset! in-step-nanos 0)\n  (reset! recent-durations [])\n  (vreset! last-machine nil)\n  (reset! load-count 0)\n  (reset! ready-count 0)\n  (reset! run-log [])\n  (reset! start-ms (System/currentTimeMillis)))\n\n(defn- counted-step\n  [machine]\n  (let [n (swap! steps inc)]\n    (when (= n 1) (println :STEP-STARTED) (flush))\n    (vreset! last-machine machine)\n    (let [t0 (System/nanoTime)\n          v (original-step machine)\n          t1 (System/nanoTime)\n          d (- t1 t0)]\n      (swap! in-step-nanos + d)\n      (swap! recent-durations (fn [r] (vec (take-last 64 (conj r d)))))\n      v)))\n\n(defn- instrumented-run-on-stream\n  [session ready? load run]\n  (let [ready?* (fn [c] (swap! ready-count inc) (ready? c))\n        load* (fn [c batch] (swap! load-count inc) (load c batch))\n        run* (fn [c]\n               (let [before @steps]\n                 (try\n                   (let [v (run c)]\n                     (swap! run-log conj {:entry-steps before\n                                          :exit-steps @steps\n                                          :threw false})\n                     v)\n                   (catch Throwable t\n                     (swap! run-log conj {:entry-steps before\n                                          :exit-steps @steps\n                                          :threw (ex-message t)})\n                     (throw t)))))]\n    (original-run-on-stream session ready?* load* run*)))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- state capture\n\n(defn- bounded-str\n  [x]\n  (let [s (pr-str x)]\n    (if (> (count s) 240) (str (subs s 0 240) \"…\") s)))\n\n(defn- instruction-at\n  \"The register instruction the machine's :control points at — op and\n  operands, bounded. The instruction vector is static code, so its size is\n  the compiler's, not the machine's.\"\n  [machine]\n  (try\n    (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control machine)\n          image (get (:code machine) segment)]\n      (if (and image (number? pc) (vector? (:vector image)))\n        (bounded-str (try (nth (:vector image) pc)\n                          (catch Exception e\n                            {:nth-failed (ex-message e)})))\n        {:segment segment :pc pc :image (nil? image)}))\n    (catch Exception e {:unreadable (ex-message e)})))\n\n(defn- machine-snapshot\n  \"Bounded view of one machine: no closures, no environments, no stores.\"\n  [m]\n  (when m\n    (let [k (:k m)\n          top (when (vector? k) (peek k))]\n      {:halted? (:halted? m)\n       :blocked? (:blocked? m)\n       :cont-depth (if (vector? k) (count k) (when k 1))\n       :control (when-let [c (:control m)] (select-keys c [:segment :pc]))\n       :control-inst (instruction-at m)\n       :top-frame (when (map? top) (select-keys top [:type :segment :pc :rd]))\n       :wait-set (count (or (:wait-set m) []))\n       :ready-queue (count (or (:ready-queue m) []))\n       :window-size (count (:window m))\n       :value (bounded-str (:value m))})))\n\n(defn- duration-stats\n  []\n  (let [rs @recent-durations]\n    (when (seq rs)\n      (let [sorted (sort rs)]\n        {:n (count sorted)\n         :min-ns (first sorted)\n         :p50-ns (nth sorted (quot (count sorted) 2))\n         :max-ns (last sorted)}))))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage A\n\n(defn- make-load-rows\n  []\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader\n    (fn [m rows stamp]\n      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n      (semantic/load-vector m\n                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n                            vm/semantic-contract))\n    vm/ast-contract))\n\n(defn- old-probe-bounded-run\n  \"Round 1's runner, verbatim semantics.\"\n  [machine]\n  (loop [v machine n 0]\n    (cond\n      (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n      (= n 2000000)\n      (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n                      {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\n      :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n)))))\n\n(defn- stage-a-vacuity\n  \"Reproduce round 1's evaluator-session drive exactly — including its\n  missing queue step — and measure how many steps it actually executed.\"\n  []\n  (println :STAGE-A :round-1-probe-reproduction\n           {:medium :empty-at-start :queue :absent-as-in-round-1})\n  (flush)\n  (reset-instrumentation!)\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        ;; round 1 compiled the fixture and never used the result; the call\n        ;; itself is kept so stage A matches that run's cost shape\n        _ ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n        lm (deref #'compiler-test/library-modules)\n        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n                                     :modules lm})\n        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)]\n    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n      (let [done (observer/run-on-stream session\n                                         engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                         (make-load-rows)\n                                         old-probe-bounded-run)]\n        (println :STAGE-A-RESULT\n                 {:steps @steps\n                  :loads @load-count\n                  :halted (vm/halted? (:consumer done))\n                  :blocked (vm/blocked? (:consumer done))\n                  :verdict (if (zero? @steps)\n                             :VACUOUS-no-program-ever-loaded\n                             :REAL-round1-was-valid)})\n        (flush)))))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage B\n\n(def ^:private tick-ms 10000)\n(def ^:private wall-cap-ms 1800000)\n(def ^:private frozen-ticks 3)\n\n(defn- print-tick\n  [t steps-prev]\n  (let [n @steps\n        in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n        elapsed (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) 1000)\n        m @last-machine\n        k (:k m)\n        stats (duration-stats)\n        rate (if (>= steps-prev 0)\n               (quot (* (- n steps-prev) 1000) t)\n               :first-tick)]\n    (println :TICK {:s elapsed :steps n :in-step-ms in-step-ms\n                    :steps-per-s-last-tick rate\n                    :step-ns stats\n                    :cont-depth (when (vector? k) (count k))\n                    :loads @load-count :runs (count @run-log)})\n    (flush)\n    n))\n\n(defn- dump-state\n  [worker label]\n  (println label {:steps @steps\n                  :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n                  :loads @load-count\n                  :ready-checks @ready-count\n                  :runs @run-log\n                  :entering-machine (machine-snapshot @last-machine)})\n  (when worker\n    (println :WORKER-STACK)\n    (doseq [frame (take 60 (.getStackTrace worker))]\n      (println \"  \" (str frame)))\n    (flush)))\n\n(defn- stage-b-real-path\n  []\n  (println :STAGE-B :real-kernel-c-semantic-path\n           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\n            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n            :step-limit 2000000\n            :wall-cap-ms wall-cap-ms})\n  (flush)\n  (reset-instrumentation!)\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n        _ (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n            (println :STAGE-B-BLOCKED-AT-COMPILE\n                     (select-keys compiled [:status :blocked-by]))\n            (flush))\n        ast (:ast compiled)\n        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n        result (atom {:kind :none})\n        worker (Thread. (fn []\n                          (try\n                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                                            ast modules :semantic 2000000)]\n                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\n                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)\n                                              :value (bounded-str (vm/value machine))}))\n                            (catch Throwable t\n                              (reset! result\n                                      {:kind :threw\n                                       :class (str (class t))\n                                       :message (ex-message t)\n                                       :data-keys (vec (keys (ex-data t)))\n                                       :consumer (machine-snapshot\n                                                   (:consumer (ex-data t)))\n                                       :session-consumer (machine-snapshot\n                                                           (:consumer\n                                                             (:session (ex-data t))))})))))]\n    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n    (.setDaemon worker true)\n    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n      (.start worker)\n      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n          (cond\n            (not alive)\n            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\n                                             :steps @steps\n                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n                                             :loads @load-count\n                                             :ready-checks @ready-count\n                                             :runs @run-log))\n                (flush)\n                (condp = (:kind @result)\n                  :returned (System/exit 0)\n                  :threw (System/exit 1)\n                  (System/exit 4)))\n\n            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\n            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\n\n            (and n (= n prev))\n            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\n                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\n                  (System/exit 3))\n                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n\n            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\n\n(defn -main\n  [& _args]\n  (println :PIN {:commit \"8ea857c1+probe2\"\n                 :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n                 :lane :semantic\n                 :budget \"2M instrumented steps\"\n                 :jvm (str (System/getProperty \"java.version\"))})\n  (flush)\n  (stage-a-vacuity)\n  (stage-b-real-path))\n\n(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2\n  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n    (-main)\n    (is true)))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage C\n\n;; Stage B showed the fixture's own semantic cell completes (1.1M steps,\n;; seconds of stepping) when driven alone. The reported stalls were observed\n;; on the whole-corpus gate, so stage C drives the gate itself — every\n;; fixture's A/B/compile/walker/semantic legs — under timing wrappers and\n;; the vm/step counter, with freeze detection that dumps the worker stack\n;; wherever the run stops advancing (C lane stepping, host A/B eval, or\n;; anywhere else).\n\n(def ^:private gate-frozen-ticks 30)          ;; 5 min without a step\n(def ^:private gate-wall-cap-ms 5400000)      ;; the longest observed trial\n\n(defn- wall-ms-since\n  [t0]\n  (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0))\n\n(defn- stage-c-gate\n  []\n  (println :STAGE-C :full-differential-gate\n           {:test 'yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate\n            :freeze-ticks gate-frozen-ticks\n            :wall-cap-ms gate-wall-cap-ms})\n  (flush)\n  (reset-instrumentation!)\n  (let [gate-t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n        leg (fn [label f]\n              (fn [& args]\n                (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n                      before @steps\n                      r (apply f args)]\n                  (println :LEG label\n                           {:wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n                            :steps (- @steps before)\n                            :arg0 (bounded-str (first args))})\n                  (flush)\n                  r)))\n        orig-kernel-a (deref #'latte/kernel-a)\n        orig-kernel-b (deref #'latte/kernel-b)\n        orig-kernel-compile (deref #'latte/kernel-compile)\n        orig-kernel-c (deref #'latte/kernel-c)\n        orig-kernel-row (deref #'latte/kernel-row)\n        kernel-c* (fn [compiled lane]\n                    (let [before @steps]\n                      (println :C-ENTER {:lane lane\n                                         :at-steps before\n                                         :total-s (quot (wall-ms-since gate-t0) 1000)})\n                      (flush)\n                      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n                            r (orig-kernel-c compiled lane)]\n                        (println :C-EXIT {:lane lane\n                                          :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n                                          :steps (- @steps before)\n                                          :status (:status r)\n                                          :outcome-tag (-> r :outcome first)})\n                        (flush)\n                        r)))\n        result (atom {:kind :none})\n        worker (Thread. (fn []\n                          (try\n                            ;; test-var output goes to this process's stdout\n                            ;; on purpose: the gate's own KERNEL-FIXTURE lines\n                            ;; are the live mid-fixture progress signal.\n                            (clojure.test/test-var\n                              #'yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate)\n                            (reset! result {:kind :returned\n                                            :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)})\n                            (catch Throwable t\n                              (reset! result {:kind :threw\n                                              :class (str (class t))\n                                              :message (ex-message t)\n                                              :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)})))))]\n    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n    (.setDaemon worker true)\n    (with-redefs-fn {#'vm/step counted-step\n                     #'observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream\n                     #'latte/kernel-a (leg :a orig-kernel-a)\n                     #'latte/kernel-b (leg :b orig-kernel-b)\n                     #'latte/kernel-compile (leg :compile orig-kernel-compile)\n                     #'latte/kernel-c kernel-c*\n                     #'latte/kernel-row (leg :row orig-kernel-row)}\n      (fn []\n        (.start worker)\n        (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n          (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n          (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n                n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n            (cond\n              (not alive)\n              (do (println :GATE-DONE (assoc @result\n                                             :steps @steps\n                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n                                             :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)\n                                             :runs @run-log))\n                  (flush)\n                  (condp = (:kind @result)\n                    :returned (System/exit 0)\n                    :threw (System/exit 1)\n                    (System/exit 4)))\n\n              (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) gate-t0) (long gate-wall-cap-ms))\n              (do (dump-state worker :GATE-WALL-CAP-REACHED) (System/exit 2))\n\n              (and n (= n prev))\n              (do (when (>= (inc frozen) gate-frozen-ticks)\n                    (dump-state worker :GATE-FROZEN-5MIN)\n                    (System/exit 3))\n                  (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n\n              :else (recur (or n prev) 0))))))))\n\n(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-gate\n  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n    (stage-c-gate)\n    (is true)))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage D\n\n;; The in-gate freeze sat in check-assume-have-discharge's WALKER cell: it\n;; consumed exactly its whole 2,000,000-step budget and then the run never\n;; returned while no step advanced. Stage D drives that one cell in\n;; isolation — same driver, same instrumentation — to (a) confirm the\n;; exhaustion reproduces without the corpus context and (b) capture the\n;; bounded exhaustion state: the advanced :consumer's halted/blocked flags,\n;; continuation depth, control, and the top frame.\n\n(defn- stage-d-walker\n  []\n  (println :STAGE-D :walker-cell-in-isolation\n           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\n            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n            :step-limit 2000000})\n  (flush)\n  (reset-instrumentation!)\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n        ast (:ast compiled)\n        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n        result (atom {:kind :none})\n        worker (Thread. (fn []\n                          (try\n                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                                            ast modules :walker 2000000)]\n                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\n                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)}))\n                            (catch Throwable t\n                              (reset! result\n                                      {:kind :threw\n                                       :class (str (class t))\n                                       :message (ex-message t)\n                                       :data-keys (vec (keys (ex-data t)))\n                                       :consumer (machine-snapshot\n                                                   (:consumer (ex-data t)))\n                                       :session-consumer (machine-snapshot\n                                                           (:consumer\n                                                             (:session (ex-data t))))})))))]\n    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n    (.setDaemon worker true)\n    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n      (.start worker)\n      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n          (cond\n            (not alive)\n            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\n                                             :steps @steps\n                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n                                             :loads @load-count\n                                             :runs @run-log))\n                (flush)\n                (condp = (:kind @result)\n                  :returned (System/exit 0)\n                  :threw (System/exit 1)\n                  (System/exit 4)))\n\n            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\n            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\n\n            (and n (= n prev))\n            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\n                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\n                  (System/exit 3))\n                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n\n            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\n\n(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker\n  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n    (stage-d-walker)\n    (is true)))\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage F\n\n;; The walker cell now exhausts 2M (stage D) while the semantic cell\n;; completes at 1.1M (stage B). How far over the budget is the walker?\n;; One bounded diagnostic trial at 8M — the H3-1 round's authorized trial\n;; ladder — reporting the walker's true completion count, or a second\n;; exhaustion. Diagnostic configuration only: NOT an acceptance-budget\n;; proposal.\n\n(defn- stage-f-walker-8m\n  []\n  (println :STAGE-F :walker-cell-8m-trial\n           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\n            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n            :step-limit 8000000})\n  (flush)\n  (reset-instrumentation!)\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n        ast (:ast compiled)\n        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n        result (atom {:kind :none})\n        worker (Thread. (fn []\n                          (try\n                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                                            ast modules :walker 8000000)]\n                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\n                                              :steps @steps\n                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)\n                                              :value (bounded-str (vm/value machine))}))\n                            (catch Throwable t\n                              (reset! result\n                                      {:kind :threw\n                                       :class (str (class t))\n                                       :message (ex-message t)\n                                       :steps @steps})))))]\n    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n    (.setDaemon worker true)\n    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n      (.start worker)\n      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n          (cond\n            (not alive)\n            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\n                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n                                             :loads @load-count\n                                             :runs @run-log))\n                (flush)\n                (condp = (:kind @result)\n                  :returned (System/exit 0)\n                  :threw (System/exit 1)\n                  (System/exit 4)))\n\n            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\n            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\n\n            (and n (= n prev))\n            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\n                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\n                  (System/exit 3))\n                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n\n            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\n\n(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker-8m\n  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n    (stage-f-walker-8m)\n    (is true)))\n(ns d2-wedge-min-repro\n  \"The minimized reproduction of the H3-1 'wedge' — which is a false\n  negative, not a cycle.\n\n  What round 1 measured as 'the evaluator session terminates': a probe that\n  built `semantic/create-vm` + `tu/make-observer-session` and called\n  `observer/run-on-stream` — but never appended the fixture to the session\n  medium (no `tu/queue-rows!`). An observer session over an empty medium\n  loads nothing and runs nothing, and a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true`\n  before any program (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm mints `:halted? true`), so\n  the probe read 'halted, zero budget spent' off a machine that never\n  executed an instruction.\n\n  This file is the A/B/C pair that isolates it, each arm runnable alone:\n\n    arm A  reproduces round 1's drive exactly — 0 steps, halted=true,\n           the false negative in three lines\n    arm B  adds the ONE missing line (tu/queue-rows!) and drives the same\n           D2-compiled fixture through the same evaluator session: it\n           completes under the 2M budget with the correct outcome —\n           there is no non-terminating cycle in the evaluator session,\n           the observer coordination, or any encoder layer\n    arm C  shrinks the budget to 10000 steps and shows run-bounded's\n           exhaustion throw PROPAGATES out of observer/run-on-stream\n           (carry-session rethrows; it never feeds the loop), carrying\n           the advanced machine under :consumer and the partial session\n           under :session — the opt-in recovery data, not a retry cycle.\n\n  The kernel-c semantic path (`run-guest-machine`) has no encoder session\n  in it at any commit: it is tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! +\n  observer/run-on-stream, single stage. The two C lanes differ only in\n  machine construction and loader.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\n(def steps (atom 0))\n\n(defn- counted-step\n  [machine]\n  (swap! steps inc)\n  (original-step machine))\n\n(defn- fixture-ast\n  \"The D2-compiled check-assume-have-discharge fixture, as kernel-c sees it.\"\n  []\n  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)]\n    (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n      (throw (ex-info \"fixture no longer compiles\" {:status (:status compiled)})))\n    (:ast compiled)))\n\n(defn- load-rows\n  []\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader\n    (fn [m rows stamp]\n      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n      (semantic/load-vector m\n                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n                            vm/semantic-contract))\n    vm/ast-contract))\n\n(defn- bounded-run\n  \"run-guest-machine's runner, verbatim.\"\n  [step-limit]\n  (fn [machine]\n    (loop [v machine n 0]\n      (cond\n        (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n        (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n                                         {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\n        :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n))))))\n\n(defn- bounded [x]\n  (let [s (pr-str x)]\n    (if (> (count s) 200) (subs s 0 200) s)))\n\n(defn- arm-a-round-1-drive\n  []\n  (reset! steps 0)\n  (let [machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n                                     :modules (deref #'compiler-test/library-modules)})\n        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)] ;; medium is EMPTY\n    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\n      (let [done (observer/run-on-stream session\n                                         engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                         (load-rows)\n                                         (bounded-run 2000000))]\n        {:steps @steps\n         :halted (vm/halted? (:consumer done))\n         :blocked (vm/blocked? (:consumer done))\n         :queue-line :absent}))))\n\n(defn- arm-b-true-drive\n  []\n  (reset! steps 0)\n  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n                                     :modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)})\n        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)]\n    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\n      (let [done (as-> session s\n                  (tu/queue-rows! s ast) ;; <- the ONE line round 1 omitted\n                  (observer/run-on-stream s engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                          (load-rows) (bounded-run 2000000)))\n            m (:consumer done)]\n        {:steps @steps\n         :halted (vm/halted? m)\n         :blocked (vm/blocked? m)\n         :outcome (bounded (vm/value m))}))))\n\n(defn- arm-c-exhaustion-propagates\n  []\n  (reset! steps 0)\n  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n                                     :modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)})\n        session (tu/queue-rows! (tu/make-observer-session machine) ast)]\n    (try\n      (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\n        (observer/run-on-stream session engine/ready-for-ingress?\n                                (load-rows) (bounded-run 10000))\n        {:propagated false})\n      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n        (let [d (ex-data e)\n              consumer (:consumer d)]\n          {:propagated true\n           :message (ex-message e)\n           :data-has-consumer (contains? d :consumer)\n           :data-has-session (contains? d :session)\n           :consumer-advanced {:halted (:halted? consumer)\n                               :blocked (:blocked? consumer)\n                               :cont-depth (count (:k consumer))\n                               :control (select-keys (:control consumer) [:segment :pc])}\n           :cause-preserved (some? (ex-cause e))})))))\n\n(defn- arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism\n  \"What the gate does with the exhaustion throw: kernel-attempt's catch\n  expands the exception data with `evidence-data` — dissoc'ing :session but\n  NOT :consumer, which after a full 2M-step run is the entire advanced\n  machine. This arm reproduces exactly that expansion in isolation, under a\n  wall bound with a stack dump, so the gate's post-exhaustion freeze is\n  attributable without running the corpus.\"\n  []\n  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\n    (try\n      (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast modules :walker 2000000)\n      {:exhausted false}\n      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n        (let [data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session)  ;; kernel-attempt's own dissoc\n              evidence (deref #'latte/evidence-data)\n              t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n              result (atom {:finished false})\n              worker (doto (Thread. (fn []\n                                      (try\n                                        (let [v (evidence data)]\n                                          (reset! result\n                                                  {:finished true\n                                                   :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n                                                   :walked-keys (count v)}))\n                                        (catch Throwable t\n                                          (reset! result\n                                                  {:finished true\n                                                   :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n                                                   :threw (ex-message t)})))))\n                          (.setName \"arm-d-evidence-walk\")\n                          (.setDaemon true))]\n          (.start worker)\n          (loop [waited 0]\n            (Thread/sleep 5000)\n            (let [r @result]\n              (cond\n                (:finished r) r\n\n                (>= waited 120000)\n                (do (println :ARM-D-UNFINISHED-AFTER-MS waited)\n                    (doseq [frame (take 25 (.getStackTrace worker))]\n                      (println \"  \" (str frame)))\n                    (flush)\n                    {:finished false :capped-at-ms waited})\n\n                :else (recur (+ waited 5000))))))))))\n\n(defn- cycle-scan\n  \"Identity-based DFS over the same shapes evidence-data/postwalk traverse\n  (maps, vectors, seqs, sets, records). Reports unique node count, the\n  deepest sharing, and — decisively — whether any container re-enters a node\n  already on the DFS path: that is a true cycle, on which clojure.walk's\n  postwalk (no seen-set) never terminates. Sharing off the path is normal\n  persistent-structure DAG sharing and terminates.\"\n  [x]\n  (let [seen (java.util.IdentityHashMap.)\n        path (java.util.IdentityHashMap.)\n        nodes (atom 0)\n        shared (atom 0)\n        cycle (atom nil)\n        container? (fn [v] (or (map? v) (vector? v) (sequential? v) (set? v) (record? v)))\n        children (fn [v]\n                   (cond\n                     (map? v) (concat (keys v) (vals v))\n                     (record? v) (vals v)\n                     :else (seq v)))]\n    (letfn [(go [v depth]\n              (when (> depth 200000) (throw (ex-info \"scan depth cap\" {:depth depth})))\n              (when (container? v)\n                (when (.containsKey path v)\n                  (when-not @cycle (reset! cycle {:type (str (class v)) :at-depth depth}))\n                  nil)\n                (if (.containsKey seen v)\n                  (do (swap! shared inc) nil)\n                  (do (.put seen v true)\n                      (.put path v true)\n                      (swap! nodes inc)\n                      (doseq [c (children v)] (go c (inc depth)))\n                      (.remove path v)))))]\n      (try\n        (go x 0)\n        (catch Throwable t {:scan-threw (ex-message t)}))\n      {:unique-containers @nodes\n       :shared-revisits @shared\n       :cycle @cycle})))\n\n(defn- arm-e-cycle-scan\n  \"Scan the exhausted machine itself (the :consumer from arm D's throw) for\n  a cycle with the identity DFS above — the difference between an expensive\n  finite expansion and a non-terminating one.\"\n  []\n  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\n    (try\n      (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast modules :walker 2000000)\n      {:exhausted false}\n      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n        (cycle-scan (:consumer (ex-data e)))))))\n\n(defn -main\n  [& _args]\n  (println :PIN {:commit \"8ea857c1+min-repro\" :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge})\n  (println :ARM-A (arm-a-round-1-drive))\n  (println :ARM-B (arm-b-true-drive))\n  (println :ARM-C (arm-c-exhaustion-propagates))\n  (println :ARM-D (arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism))\n  (println :ARM-E (arm-e-cycle-scan))\n  (flush))\n\n(deftest test-h31-wedge-min-repro\n  (testing \"diagnostic reproduction only — contributes zero coverage\"\n    (let [a (arm-a-round-1-drive)\n          _ (println :ARM-A a)\n          b (arm-b-true-drive)\n          _ (println :ARM-B b)\n          c (arm-c-exhaustion-propagates)\n          _ (println :ARM-C c)\n          d (arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism)\n          _ (println :ARM-D d)\n          e (arm-e-cycle-scan)\n          _ (println :ARM-E e)]\n      (is (zero? (:steps a)) \"arm A reproduces the round-1 false negative: no step ever ran\")\n      (is (and (:halted a) (not (:blocked a)))\n          \"arm A's machine reads halted only because create-vm mints :halted? true\")\n      (is (and (:halted b) (pos? (:steps b)) (< (:steps b) 2000000))\n          \"arm B: the same session with the fixture queued completes under the budget\")\n      (is (and (:propagated c) (:data-has-consumer c) (:data-has-session c))\n          \"arm C: the budget throw escapes run-on-stream carrying its recovery data\")\n      (is (map? d) \"arm D reports the post-exhaustion evidence walk's cost shape\")\n      (is (map? e) \"arm E reports the exhausted machine's cycle scan\")\n      (flush))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
