{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: ACCEPT for landing at `a252a8a0`.** The D2 merge to master is cleared. The kernel gate remains `:blocked` for the 20 unexercised arities, as ruled.\n\nThe revised assertion in [clojure_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-h31/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1397) detects the previously missed outcome: `tree-seq` reaches the sentinel through the error vector, maps, map entries, and nested callee vector. The supplied mutation result confirms that it fails on both evaluator lanes for that defect. If an `ExceptionInfo` is caught and rendered as a string, the preceding assertion rejects that result because it is not an error vector.\n\nThere is a limit to the claim: `tree-seq coll? seq` cannot inspect metadata, strings, or arbitrary non-collection wrappers, and a returned sentinel alone cannot prove that every conceivable future execution path preserves evidence of body entry. For the reviewed call path and the supplied mutation, however, the body’s returned keyword is carried in ordinary outcome data; I found no path in this change that hides it in those forms. The comment’s “passes only when the body never ran” is broader than the assertion can establish in general, but that overstatement does not block this fix.\n\nThe complete diff changes only that test and deletes `test/d2_wedge_probe.clj`. The deleted file is the round-1 probe: it compiled the fixture but did not queue it. [d2_wedge_probe2.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-h31/test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj:1) reproduces and diagnoses that vacuous drive, and [d2_wedge_min_repro.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-h31/test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj:1) supplies the minimized comparison.\n\nThe prior standing-bar verdict therefore carries forward: unary entry, guard order, refusal without body application, guest-unbindable token, dynamic admission, the 100k bound, and the merged evidence harness all passed at `c6bd6d79`; this test-only diff changes no compiler or evidence-harness implementation. I relied on the supplied remote results for dynamic checks and ran no test suites locally."}}
